From 165a1d25bbb4b0acf1ecf6a02a0723d0be89ea6c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nicole Muzzin <nicks@fuckin.email>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 01:44:33 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] editing: forwardDelete, insertLineBreak and Chrome's typed
 white space

The Delete key and Shift+Enter did nothing in editing hosts, and spaces typed
before text stayed no-break spaces ("abc&nbsp;x").

Implement the forwardDelete and insertLineBreak commands from the editing
spec, for execCommand and for the Delete key (deleteContentForward) and
Shift+Enter (insertLineBreak). Forward deletion at the end of the editing host
stops there instead of extending the selection out of it.

insertText now canonicalizes white space at both ends of the inserted text, as
the spec's steps 15 and 16 do, without deleting collapsed spaces so a second
space typed at the end of a line is kept, as in Chrome. The start scan of
canonicalize whitespace now repeats over the whole run of spaces as the spec
says, instead of stopping after one.

Like Chrome, text typed on a line holding only a placeholder <br> replaces it,
and a deletion that leaves the caret after a <br> ending its block adds a
placeholder <br> so the emptied last line stays.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
